Learning GitHub Actions – Day 1: Workflows


📌 What is a Workflow?
A workflow is an automated process defined in a YAML file. It can run when specific events occur in a GitHub repository, such as pushing code or creating a pull request.

🛠️ What I'm learning:
How workflows are defined in a .github/workflows/ directory.
How to configure workflow triggers.
How automation starts when a specified event occurs.

💡 Key Takeaway: Workflows are the foundation of GitHub Actions and help automate repetitive development tasks.
One concept at a time, one step closer to mastering DevOps! 💻
